# This is a Initial Reimplementation of ArvorCTL in ZTSL-26
def_mod libztsl # basically ztsl. ztc ignores this and compiles THIS ↓
ztsl.start
}
func check_root
ccompat
```c
if (getuid() != 0) {
    fprintf(stderr, "E: This Command needs Root Privileges.\n");
    fflush(stderr);
    exit(1);
}
```
}
func help
run.func check_root
if argument is not defined
then
text.show
```
Usage: arvorctl [command] [options]

Commands:
  snapshot [name]        Create a new snapshot of root through nsm (auto-named if omitted)
  rollback <name>        Roll back the root volume to the specified snapshot through nsm
  help                   Show this help message
```
}
func create
run.func check_root
if argument snapshot is passed with %ea%
then
sys.exec
```
/usr/bin/nsm create %ea%
```
if result is =! 0
then
text.show
```
E: failed to create snapshot
```
}
func rollback
run.func check_root
if argument rollback is passed with %ea%
then
sys.exec.silent
```exec
/usr/bin/nsm rollback %ea%
```
if result is = 0
then
text.show
```
Rollback of %ea% done. A Reboot is recommended.
```
if argument is not defined
then 
text.show
```
E : unknown command %a%
```
run.func help
}
func help_command
if argument help is passed
then
run.func help
}
ztsl.end
